| BuildROM: build the ROM image for RISC OS on Linux (RISCOS.IMG) on a
| Raspberry Pi running RISC OS, with RISC OS Open's DDE.
|
| Before running it:
|  - the DDE installed as its ReadMe says (AcornC/C++ beside !Boot, and
|    Developer.!SysMerge run), and AcornC/C++.!SetPaths seen by the Filer
|    (or run), so that cc, objasm, link and amu are on Run$Path;
|  - this folder (ROLSrc) on a hard disc or SD card (not RAM:), with about
|    1GB free for the build.
|
| Run it from a task window (Ctrl-F12) or the command line (F12):
|    *Obey <path>.ROLSrc.BuildROM
| That does all the phases. To redo only some of them, list them, e.g.
|    *Obey <path>.ROLSrc.BuildROM rom install_rom join
|
| The result is ROLSrc.RiscOS.Images.rom: copy it to the Linux card as
| /opt/riscos/RISCOS.IMG (keep the old one). The log is ROLSrc.BuildLog.
|
| Adapted from Unix.LinuxSupport.Build (Timothy Baldwin, Apache 2.0),
| which does the same inside RISC OS for Linux.
|
| Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Youll. Apache License 2.0.

Set ROLSrc$Dir <Obey$Dir>
If "<SetPaths$Dir>" = "" Then Error Let the Filer see AcornC/C++.!SetPaths (or run it) first: the DDE's tools must be on Run$Path
RMEnsure UtilityModule 5.00 Error RISC OS 5 is needed
IfThere <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.BuildSys.Components.ROOL.Linux Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Error BuildROM must be in ROLSrc, beside the RiscOS and mixed folders

| Files that have gone missing in unzipping before now
IfThere <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Sources.Programmer.HdrSrc.hdr.IO.IOMD Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Error ROLSrc.RiscOS.Sources.Programmer.HdrSrc.hdr.IO.IOMD is missing: unzip ROLSrc again
IfThere <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Sources.Lib.CLXLite.c.wildcard Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Error ROLSrc.RiscOS.Sources.Lib.CLXLite.c.wildcard is missing: unzip ROLSrc again
IfThere <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Sources.Lib.CLXLite.h.wildcard Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Error ROLSrc.RiscOS.Sources.Lib.CLXLite.h.wildcard is missing: unzip ROLSrc again


WimpSlot 32M
Set Wimp$ScrapDir <ROLSrc$Dir>.Scrap
CDir <Wimp$ScrapDir>

Dir <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS

Set Alias$IconSprites ||
Set Alias$egrep grep -E %%*0
Set Alias$Unix.egrep grep -E %%*0
Set Build$Image rom
Set Build$Imagename rom
SetEval SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH 0
X Do SetEval ROOL$MaxJobs 1

Set ROLSrc$DDECLib <CLIB$Path>
| DDE 32d's !SetPaths reaches its tools through Tools: (Tools$Dir), which
| Env.!Common below points at ROLSrc's Library instead: amu, cc and the
| rest were then "not found". So put the DDE's tool folders on Run$Path
| by name (31d did this itself).
Set Run$Path <Run$Path>,<SetPaths$Dir>.Lib32.,<SetPaths$Dir>.Lib32.Build.,<SetPaths$Dir>.Lib32.Unix.
Obey <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Env.ROOL.Linux
| Host tools (built and run on this machine during the build) link with
| Build$HostLibs. RISC OS Open's build fills Library.Acorn.HostLibs from a
| separate BuildHost build; without that, use the DDE's own libraries.
| (ROLSrc$DDECLib is the DDE's CLIB$Path, saved before Env.ROOL.Linux
| replaced it.)
IfThere <Build$HostLibs>.CLib.o.stubs Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Set Build$HostLibs <ROLSrc$DDECLib>^
IfThere <Build$HostLibs>.CLib.o.stubs Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Set Build$HostLibs <C/C++$Dir>.Export.APCS-32.Lib
IfThere <Build$HostLibs>.CLib.o.stubs Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Set Build$HostLibs <SetPaths$Dir>.^.Export.APCS-32.Lib
IfThere <Build$HostLibs>.CLib.o.stubs Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Set Build$HostLibs <SetPaths$Dir>.^.Libraries
IfThere <Build$HostLibs>.CLib.o.stubs Then Set ROLSrc$OK 1 Else Set ROLSrc$OK 0
If ROLSrc$OK = 0 Then Error Can't find the DDE's C library (CLib.o.stubs). Tried <ROLSrc$DDECLib>^ and under <SetPaths$Dir>.^ (Export.APCS-32.Lib, Libraries)
Echo Host tools use <Build$HostLibs>
| RISC OS Open's srcbuild itself (not any srcbuild wrapper earlier on the path).
| The phases are written out in full: srcbuild doesn't expand <variables>
| in its arguments.
| Edit is linked for its address in the ROM, and its makefile doesn't
| relink it when that address moves in a build over an earlier one (the
| ROM then says "ROM application !Edit cannot be RAM loaded"). So it is
| linked afresh every time.
X Remove <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Sources.Apps.EditApp.linked.!RunImage
X Remove <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Sources.Apps.EditApp.linked.!RunImage_sym
Spool <ROLSrc$Dir>.BuildLog
If "%*0" = "" Then /<ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Library.Build.srcbuild -s export_hdrs export_libs resources rom install_rom join
If "%*0" <> "" Then /<ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Library.Build.srcbuild -s %*0
Spool
Echo
Echo Finished. If there were no errors (see <ROLSrc$Dir>.BuildLog)
Echo the ROM is <ROLSrc$Dir>.RiscOS.Images.rom
